2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"H001081","fullName":"Rep. Hayes, Jahana [D-CT-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CT"},{"bioguideId":"W000830","fullName":"Rep. Whitesides, George [D-CA-27]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"C001061","fullName":"Rep. Cleaver, Emanuel [D-MO-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MO"},{"bioguideId":"M001223","fullName":"Rep. Magaziner, Seth [D-RI-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"RI"},{"bioguideId":"W000788","fullName":"Rep. Williams, Nikema [D-GA-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"GA"},{"bioguideId":"V000138","fullName":"Rep. Vindman, Eugene Simon [D-VA-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"C001080","fullName":"Rep. Chu, Judy [D-CA-28]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"W000797","fullName":"Rep. Wasserman Schultz, Debbie [D-FL-25]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"},{"bioguideId":"S001200","fullName":"Rep. Soto, Darren [D-FL-9]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"},{"bioguideId":"C001131","fullName":"Rep. Casar, Greg [D-TX-35]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"N000188","fullName":"Rep. Norcross, Donald [D-NJ-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"},{"bioguideId":"B001278","fullName":"Rep. Bonamici, Suzanne [D-OR-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OR"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-11-18T18:40:04+00:00","id":"hr8915-119","introducedDate":"2026-05-20","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-05-20","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"laws":[],"number":"8915","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Commerce","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"S000168","district":27,"fullName":"Rep. Salazar, Maria Elvira [R-FL-27]","party":"R","state":"FL"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2026-05-20","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Nurture Originals, Foster Art, and Keep Entertainment Safe Act of 2026 or the NO FAKES Act of 2026</strong></p><p>This bill creates a federal intellectual property right to protect individuals from unauthorized digital replicas (e.g., digital content made using generative artificial intelligence) of their voice and visual likeness.</p><p>Specifically, the bill gives each individual or right holder the right to authorize the use of the individual's voice or visual likeness (1) in a digital replica, or (2)&nbsp;for a product or service requiring authorization to avoid liability&nbsp;under the bill. This property right is not assignable during the individual’s lifetime but is licensable and does not expire upon the death of the individual.</p><p>Generally, any individual or entity that engages in specified prohibited activities (e.g., distributing a digital replica without authorization) shall be liable in a civil action and subject to related penalties.&nbsp;The bill exempts specified uses from liability, such as categories of conduct likely to involve protected speech under the First Amendment (e.g., news reporting, sports broadcasts, and satire).</p><p>The bill establishes (1) a notice-and-takedown process for unauthorized digital replicas; and (2) a counter-notification process, which allows an individual to contest the removal of a digital replica. The bill establishes penalties related to&nbsp;false or deceptive notice or counter-notice.</p><p>The bill expressly preempts state laws related to digital replicas&nbsp;except for causes of action under state statutes or common law in existence as of January 2, 2025.</p>","updateDate":"2026-07-17T20:53:20Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"NO FAKES Act of 2026","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-11-18T09:06:45Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-11-18T09:06:45Z"}
